WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.401
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:12.704 --> 00:00:13.870
PROFESSOR: Have you enjoyed?

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:14.453
AUDIENCE: Yes.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:18.870
PROFESSOR: OK.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:23.560
We have a little business today
that has to do with the class.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.900
And then I want to take
off my academic hat

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.260
and tell you things that I
wish somebody had told me

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.830
when I was graduating.

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:37.200
I won't be able to
tell you all of them,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:40.080
I'm sure, because I could
go on for hours with things

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:43.330
that I wish I had been
told at some point.

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:47.590
But we'll get in
as many as we can.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:51.120
So let's start with that which
had to do with the class.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:56.160
I promised you a demonstration
that you would remember,

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:02.430
perhaps, forever and that is
very much related to something

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:04.500
that you studied.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:10.600
But we'll put a different
light on the effects.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.840
And we'll talk about that.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:16.507
What we have is a recording--

00:01:16.507 --> 00:01:18.840
very poor quality, but that
doesn't make any difference.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:22.290
It was made about 30 years
ago in my living room.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:23.790
We had a very--

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:25.530
we had this 1/8
of a sphere, which

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:31.520
was really well equalized,
well-designed by any standard.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:38.730
And we decided to find out what
a room really did to things.

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:45.300
Like the sound we produced from
a loud speaker or from you.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:50.100
And we made this
recording, played it

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:54.480
through the loudspeaker, put a
microphone in normal listening

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:58.490
position in the living room,
took what was on the mic--

00:01:58.490 --> 00:01:59.620
when was recorded.

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:02.580
And we recorded what
went into the microphone,

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:05.040
put it back into the speaker.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.580
Came through again, recorded,
put it back into the speaker.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:11.160
Came through again,
up to six times.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:15.120
And I think you'll hear
the first time through.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.790
Now, mind you, that's
sort of like a second time

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:19.500
through because you're
going into a room.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:22.180
Again, you're not
listening over headphones.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:25.140
The normal modes in this
room aren't the same--

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.260
at the same frequency.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:29.640
So going through the
same system twice

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:32.100
is much worse than going
through two different ones,

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:35.880
but you'll get the message.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:40.330
Basically, you'll hear
the so-called original.

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:47.100
And it's music first, speech,
next, speech sample, next.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:58.740
And a pink noise, which is equal
energy per percentage spectrum

00:02:58.740 --> 00:02:59.610
third.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:03.150
And then you'll hear, second
round with that will be--

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:04.620
after it's gone through twice.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.400
And the third time you
hear it, the three--

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:10.160
they will have gone
through six times.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:13.290
Now, what I want you
to concentrate on

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:18.570
is how each of these
sounds deteriorates as it

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:22.140
goes through this process.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:26.070
See if you can't relate
the music deterioration

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:30.730
to the speech deterioration
to the noise deterioration.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:37.740
And I will put on the board
what would seem like something

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:38.700
obvious to you.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:41.800
It may not seem so obvious by
the time the demonstration gets

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:42.300
to the end.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:46.830
I will put on a little matrix
telling which one is playing.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:47.730
So let's go.

00:03:50.399 --> 00:03:50.940
The original.

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:51.606
[AUDIO PLAYBACK]

00:03:51.606 --> 00:03:56.363
[MUSIC PLAYING]

